<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mossi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mossi are a people of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burkina-faso">Burkina Faso</a>, who founded a group of kingdoms in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volta-river">Volta</a> basin from the fifteenth century. Mossi cavalry raided northwards into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-bend">Niger bend</a>. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a>'s profile, Mossi raids were among the external pressures that weakened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>.</p></div>
